{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "ReadReceiptSheet: the read list of one of the viewer's group messages, two columns that page on their own. Input `readers` / `unread` are counts of the members loaded so far (tests build r1..rN and u1..uN). `tabs` is null when the tabs are not drawn, else the two tabs in order with the number each shows (null: no number). `body`: spinner (loading), error (load failed, with a retry key), unavailable (no list for this message, no retry), list (the active column's rows), empty (the active column has no rows and no next page). `rows` is the number of member rows drawn. `tail` is the last row of a list: none, busy (a spinner, not a control), loadMore (the load-more key), retry (the load-more-failed key). `taps` are steps: tap `tail`, `retry` or `tab:<column>` and the events it emits, in order.",
  "rules": {
    "counts": "A tab's number is the summary count the host passes (readCount / unreadCount, from receipt.readSummary). Without one the tab has no number; the number is never the length of the loaded list, which may be one page.",
    "states": "state loading: the title row, both tabs (with the summary counts when given) and a spinner as the body. error: the title row and an error notice (readReceiptLoadFailed) with a retry key that emits retry; no tabs. unavailable: the title row and the notice readReceiptUnavailable; no tabs, no retry (the host uses it for NOT_FOUND and available:false). ready: the tabs and the active column.",
    "paging": "In ready, after the rows of the active column: loadingMore equal to the column → busy; else loadMoreFailed equal to the column → retry key (readReceiptLoadMoreFailed) emitting loadMore(column); else hasMore of the column → load-more key (readReceiptLoadMore) emitting loadMore(column); else nothing. A native list may also emit loadMore when the key scrolls into view. A column never asks twice while it is loading more; the other column pages on its own. A column with no rows and no next page draws its empty notice; with a next page it draws no notice, only the key.",
    "tabs": "Switching tabs emits nothing and keeps both columns (the host holds them). initialTab picks the column shown first (read by default).",
    "shell": "The sheet takes its container's width. Outside a kit overlay it draws its own card shell (radius xl, hairline border, lg shadow) at most 320 wide, shrinking with a narrower container, and its rows scroll within 320. Inside a kit BottomSheet or Modal it draws no shell, fills the surface width and declares its own header (Vue useFlareSheetOwnHeader, Compose FlareSheetOwnHeader, the same mechanism on SwiftUI / Flutter); the host opens it with the sheet's fill mode so the sheet's title is the accessible name only and the rows take the remaining height."
  },
  "strings": {
    "zh": {
      "readReceiptLoadFailed": "名单读取失败",
      "readReceiptUnavailable": "这条消息的已读名单不可查看",
      "readReceiptLoadMore": "加载更多",
      "readReceiptLoadMoreFailed": "加载失败，点按重试"
    },
    "en": {
      "readReceiptLoadFailed": "Couldn't load the list",
      "readReceiptUnavailable": "This message's read list isn't available",
      "readReceiptLoadMore": "Load more",
      "readReceiptLoadMoreFailed": "Couldn't load more. Tap to retry"
    }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "summary-counts-not-list-length",
      "platforms": [
        "vue",
        "flutter",
        "ios",
        "compose"
      ],
      "input": {
        "state": "ready",
        "readers": 2,
        "unread": 1,
        "readCount": 30,
        "unreadCount": 12,
        "readHasMore": true,
        "unreadHasMore": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "tabs": [
          {
            "value": "read",
            "count": 30
          },
          {
            "value": "unread",
            "count": 12
          }
        ],
        "body": "list",
        "rows": 2,
        "tail": "loadMore"
      },
      "taps": [
        {
          "tap": "tail",
          "emits": [
            [
              "loadMore",
              "read"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
